menu "machn (machine node) configuration"

    config MACHN_RELAY_FEEDBACK
        bool "Enable relay feedback (read-back) monitoring"
        default n
        help
            Enable the machine role's relay-feedback (read-back) monitoring:
            sampling each stop-circuit relay's switched output through a
            resistor-divider SENSE input, comparing commanded-vs-observed every
            comparator tick, raising a self-clearing relay fault on a persistent
            contradiction, and — after RELAY_FAULT_STOP_TICKS (~1 s) — forcing
            the robot STOPPED.

            DEFAULT n (DESCOPED). A new machine-specific hardware revision +
            wiring diagram is incoming on which the divider feedback voltages
            cannot be read sanely, so the read-back path is compiled out by
            default. The relay DRIVE path (both coils commanded from each core's
            own verdict) and the series de-energize-to-safe stop are unaffected
            by this option and are always built.

            Set to y to restore feedback on hardware that supports it. Before
            doing so, re-verify the RELAY_A_SENSE / RELAY_B_SENSE pin numbers,
            the divider ratios / logic levels, and RELAY_FEEDBACK_MS against the
            new wiring.

            Full rationale, reversal steps, and safety-case impact:
            docs/RELAY_FEEDBACK_DESCOPE.md.

endmenu
